    user_response: "Silsila Maktab \342\200\224 Full-Page Landing Page Design Specification (v2)\nThis document represents the complete, high-fidelity design specification for the Silsilah Maktab landing page. It combines the core design system tokens (colors, typography, buttons, tables, badges, cards, and scrollbars) with the actual page sections, layouts, and copy transcribed from the full-page product landing page screenshot.\n\nUse this specification in Google AI Studio to generate a pixel-perfect, responsive, and highly interactive landing page using HTML/Tailwind CSS or React/Tailwind CSS.\n\n1. Brand Identity & Global Style Tokens\nA. Design System Concept\nProduct Name: Silsila Maktab (branded as Silsila by Sylergy)\nTheme: Minimalist, serene, highly professional, and modern administrative software for supplementary Islamic schools (Maktabs/Madrasahs).\nCore Aesthetic: Warm off-white backgrounds, deep forest-green primary containers, and bright mint-green accents that promote feelings of growth, heritage, structure, and peace.\nB. Color Palette\nImplement these exact custom property mappings:\n\n:root {\n  --primary: #1D564B;       /* Deep Forest Green/Teal - primary headers, main cards, hero buttons */\n  --accent: #00A896;        /* Bright Mint/Teal - brand highlights, badges, primary CTA backgrounds */\n  --background: #FBF9F6;    /* Off-white/Warm Cream - global body background */\n  --card: #FFFFFF;          /* Pure White - background for elevated container components and cards */\n  --secondary: #EEEAE5;     /* Warm Light Grey - background for alternating sections or inactive elements */\n  --muted: #E5E0DA;         /* Muted Soft Grey - for subtle borders, secondary labels, and text */\n  --border: #E1DCD6;        /* Outer Structural Borders - thin card lines and table grid lines */\n  --destructive: #D9383A;   /* Overdue Red - for negative alerts, overdue invoices, and \"Absent\" statuses */\n}\nC. Typography Scale\nFont Family: Modern, highly readable sans-serif (e.g., Plus Jakarta Sans, Inter, or Outfit).\nHero Title: 3.5rem (56px) / Weight 600 / Line-height 1.2\nSection Heading: 2.25rem (36px) / Weight 600 / Line-height 1.3\nBody / Paragraph: 1.125rem (18px) / Weight 400 / Line-height 1.6\nMuted / Small: 0.875rem (14px) / Weight 400 / Line-height 1.4\nD. Spacing & Grid System\nElement Padding (--space-element): 2.5rem (40px) \342\200\224 internal card gaps, button spacing, form fields.\nBlock Grid Gap (--space-block): 5rem (80px) \342\200\224 vertical margins between columns and groups of cards.\nSection Gap (--space-section): 8.5rem (136px) \342\200\224 vertical padding (py-24 or py-32 in Tailwind) separating main page sections.\n2. Reusable UI Components\nA. Buttons & CTAs\nPrimary Mint CTA (Main Landing Page Button):\nSolid --accent background, text #FFFFFF (or dark forest green if contrast warrants). Hover: background --accent with opacity 0.9, scale up slightly on hover.\nSecondary Green CTA (Standard Action Button):\nSolid --primary background, text #FFFFFF. Hover: slight background change, smooth transition.\nOutline Button:\nTransparent background, border 1.5px solid var(--primary), text --primary.\nGhost Button:\nTransparent background, text --primary. Hover: background --secondary.\nDestructive Button:\nSolid --destructive background, text #FFFFFF. Sizes:\nDefault (Navbar/Standard): padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem; font-size: 16px;\nLarge (Hero/Banner): padding: 0.875rem 1.75rem; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600;\nB. Cards & Elevating Containers\nBasic Card: --card background, 1px solid var(--border), rounded corners (12px / 0.75rem).\nFeature Card (Hoverable): Same as basic card but on hover applies box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(29, 86, 75, 0.04) and translates translate-y-[-4px] upwards.\nHighlighted Card: Pure white card with solid border accent border-top: 4px solid var(--accent) or border-left: 4px solid var(--primary).\nC. Status Badges & Attendance Markers\nTo display administrative capabilities, mock indicators must use these exact styling formulas:\n\nPaid (Success Badge): pill style, bg #EBF7EE, border #C3EBD0, text #1E562A, label \"Paid\"\nPending (Warning Badge): pill style, bg #FFF8EC, border #FFE3B3, text #8A5E1A, label \"Pending\"\nOverdue (Destructive Badge): pill style, bg #FDF2F2, border #FAD2D2, text #9C2A2B, label \"Overdue\"\nAttendance Dot (Present - P): Circle, bg #EBF7EE, text #1E562A, font-bold, label \"P\"\nAttendance Dot (Absent - A): Circle, bg #FDF2F2, text #9C2A2B, font-bold, label \"A\"\nAttendance Dot (Late - L): Circle, bg #FFF8EC, text #8A5E1A, font-bold, label \"L\"\n3. Core Page Sections (Layout & Copy)\nImplement the landing page in a vertical sequence using the sections below. Alternating background colors are noted for visual depth.\n\nSection 1: Navigation Header (Sticky)\nBackground: --background (fully transparent on scroll with backdrop-blur)\nLayout: Centered, max-width wrapper with flex space-between.\nLogo (Left): Minimalist wordmark: Silsila (font-semibold, --primary, 1.5rem) + <span class=\"text-xs text-accent\">by Sylergy</span>.\nNav Links (Center): Product, Use Cases, Pricing, About, Staff Login, Parent Login, Register school.\nCTA (Right): Small \"Book a 15-min demo\" button in Primary Mint (--accent).\nSection 2: Hero Fold (Value Proposition & Mock Dashboard)\nBackground: --background\nLayout: Two-column layout (stacks to single-column on mobile).\nLeft Column (Text & Action):\nCategory Badge: Centered or left-aligned light pill text: FOR MADRASAHS & MAKTABS (text --accent, tracking-wider, font-bold).\nMain Heading: \"Attendance and fees, finally under control.\" (size 3.5rem, weight 600, color --primary).\nSubheading: \"Reduce admin time, collect fees faster, and give every family a reliable portal\342\200\224budget gently by WhatsApp.\"\nInline Bullet List (with checkmark icons):\n\342\234\224 Proofing registry in minutes, not hours\n\342\234\224 Verifiably faster with fewer follow-ups\n\342\234\224 Partners with standard WhatsApp and emails\nCTA Block:\nButton 1: \"Book a 15-min demo\" (Large Primary Mint Button)\nButton 2: \"See the parent portal \342\206\222\" (Ghost button with chevron arrow)\nRight Column (Dashboard Preview):\nAn interactive CSS mockup of the Silsila Administrator Dashboard:\nHeader: \"Dashboard \342\200\224 Monday, 11 Nov 2024\"\nStats Row:\nAttendance Rate: 94% (with small green sparkline or trend badge)\nFees Collected: \302\2436,280 (progress bar at 85%)\nUnpaid Invoices: \302\243410 (colored red --destructive)\nTotal Pupils: 121\nRecent Activity List:\nZahra Rahman attended Year 3 - Qur\'an (timestamp: 10 mins ago)\nFaisal Ahmed marked Late for Year 1\nFees paid for Adam Rahman (\302\24345.00)\nMonthly automated invoices generated\nSection 3: Social Proof / Testimonials Band\nBackground: --secondary (creates a soft break from the hero background)\nLayout: Clean grid of 2 prominent blockquote feature cards side-by-side.\nCard 1 Quote:\n\"Virtually, a system that understands how madrasahs actually work. The WhatsApp integration is a superb change for parent communication!\"\nAuthor: Ustadh Bilal Vance, Head Teacher, Madrasah Al-Ansar\nCard 2 Quote:\n\"We recovered our fee-chasing time significantly. Parents can give their details and look up invoices through the portal seamlessly.\"\nAuthor: Fihan Rahman, Madrasah Treasurer\nSection 4: Problem vs. Solution (\"From Chaos to Calm\")\nBackground: --primary (Deep Forest Teal - dark mode section with white text)\nHeader:\nWHAT WE SOLVE (Small, --accent uppercase label)\n\"From chaos to calm\" (Section Heading 2.25rem, color #FFFFFF)\nSubtitle: \"Madrasah admin shouldn\'t feel overwhelming. Silsila replaces fragmented tools with one simple system\342\200\224one class at a time.\"\nLayout: Two-column layout contrasting the traditional challenges vs Silsila\'s modern workflows.\nLeft Column (The Problem):\nRed accent flags:\n\342\235\214 Information stored across too many apps: Paper registers, personal WhatsApp threads, and fragile spreadsheets make tracking a heavy chore.\n\342\235\214 Fee-chasing is a constant chore: Unclear balances, missed payment deadlines, and awkward, repeating face-to-face follow-up conversations.\n\342\235\214 Parent communication feels chaotic: Crucial school updates get lost in endless community group chats; parents are left in the dark about attendance and pending invoices.\nRight Column (Silsila\'s Approach):\nGreen/Mint accent flags:\n\342\234\224 One unified, cloud-based platform: A single, beautiful web application accessible securely from any device, anytime.\n\342\234\224 Clear invoices and easy payments: Automated WhatsApp and SMS payment links with instant, elegant receipt generation.\n\342\234\224 A modern web portal for families: Parents log in with passwordless magic links to view historical attendance records, upcoming schedules, and invoices.\nSection 5: \"Built for how madrasahs work\" (The Feature Grid)\nBackground: --background\nHeader:\nTHE TOOLKIT (Small, --accent uppercase label)\n\"Built for how madrasahs work\"\nSubtitle: \"Every feature is shaped around a real workflow\342\200\224one that turns a daily administrative headache into a beautiful, quiet routine.\"\nGrid Layout: 3-column, 2-row grid of Feature Cards (Hoverable).\nCards Content:\nFast Attendance Register: Pupil registers completed in under a minute, optimized for fast mobile or desktop clicking.\nInteractive Core Stats: Access parent details, emergency contact numbers, medical notes, and classroom schedules instantly.\nInvoicing and Analysis: Generate clean receipts, track physical cash vs bank transfers, and see exactly who has paid at a glance.\nWhatsApp & SMS Links: Deliver direct payment links straight to parent phones, drastically lowering late-payment frequency.\nParent Portal: Passwordless login links let parents track attendance charts, pay fees, and view active announcements on their own.\nAudit Trails & Reports: Every invoice adjustment, fee collection, or attendance status change is timestamped and ready to export.\nSection 6: Interactive Showcase (\"See it in action\")\nBackground: --primary (Deep Forest Teal - dark mode)\nHeader:\nIN ACTION (Small, --accent uppercase label)\n\"See it in action\"\nSubtitle: \"Three perspectives, one system. Admin, teachers, and parents\342\200\224each get exactly what they need.\"\nInteractive Component:\nHorizontal selection bar representing three perspective tabs:\nTab 1: Staff - Take Attendance (Active by default)\nTab 2: Admin - Invoice + Pay Desk\nTab 3: Parent View - Fee Portal\nDynamic Content Layout:\nLeft column (Perspective copy):\nTitle: \"Mark attendance in seconds\"\nBullets:\nSee pupil class history instantly\nTap once to toggle present, absent, or late\nSubmit with one tap \342\200\224 register is automatically locked and shared with admin\nRight column (Simulated Interactive Component Mockup):\nRender the Dense Table (Weekly Attendance Grid) with custom badge status selectors:\nAdam Rahman | Mon: P | Tue: P | Wed: L | Thu: P | Fri: P\nZahra Rahman | Mon: P | Tue: A | Wed: P | Thu: P | Fri: P\nFeatures a large, solid --accent button: \"Submit Attendance Register\".\nSection 7: Proof & Quantitative Metrics (\"Fee chasing, cut by 70%\")\nBackground: --background\nHeader:\nEARLY RESULTS\n\"Fee chasing, cut by 70%\"\nSubtitle: \"Early pilots show a significant drop in administrative hours and immediate boosts to fee collection compliance.\"\nGrid of Supporting Pilot Testimonial Cards:\nCard 1: \"The attendance register is so quick now. It takes us under a minute to check in all the students.\" (\342\200\223 Teacher, Year 3)\nCard 2: \"Prior to this, we spent hours chasing invoices manually. The WhatsApp links make paying effortless for parents.\" (\342\200\223 Administrator, Al-Kauthar Academy)\nCard 3: \"I love being able to see everything on the portal\342\200\224attendance, schedules, and my invoices. No more mystery.\" (\342\200\223 Parent, Year 1 Pupil)\nSection 8: \"Simple, transparent pricing\"\nBackground: --secondary\nHeader:\nPRICING\n\"Simple, transparent pricing\"\nSubtitle: \"Pick the plan that fits your school. Prices are simple\342\200\224book a demo and we\'ll tailor it for your custom numbers.\"\nLayout: Grid of 3 pricing cards. Highlight the center card (Standard) to make it stand out.\nTiers:\nStarter (For small, newly established weekend schools)\nPrice: \302\24329 / month\nFeatures: Up to 50 active students, Daily attendance register, Basic reporting, Standard email support.\nCTA: \"Book a 15-min demo \342\206\222\" (Outline Button)\nStandard (Most Popular - Featured)\nVisuals: Primary accent header border (border-top: 4px solid var(--accent)), subtle drop shadow.\nPrice: \302\24349 / month\nFeatures: Up to 150 active students, Advanced attendance registry, Automated invoicing & tracking, WhatsApp/SMS direct payment links, Basic family dashboard, Priority email/phone support.\nCTA: \"Book a 15-min demo \342\206\222\" (Solid Primary Mint Button)\nPro (For large schools and established Madrasah networks)\nPrice: \302\24399 / month\nFeatures: Unlimited active students, Everything in Standard, Automated invoice reminders, Multi-site campus support, Custom integrations, Dedicated onboarding account manager.\nCTA: \"Book a 15-min demo \342\206\222\" (Outline Button)\nSection 9: \"A chain unbroken\" (Philosophy & Mission)\nBackground: --background\nHeader:\nOUR MISSION\n\"A chain unbroken\"\nSubtitle: \"Silsilah means an unbroken chain\342\200\224the link between family, teacher, and madrasah. We build tools to strengthen this connection, so teachers can focus on teaching.\"\nLayout: 3-column block detailing values:\nColumn 1: Deep Tradition, Modern Tech \342\200\224 Designed by developers who have run Maktabs, bridging classic Islamic supplementary school dynamics with streamlined web workflows.\nColumn 4: Low Connectivity Friendly \342\200\224 Highly optimized client-side code that works gracefully on weak mobile cellular connections or older parent devices.\nColumn 5: Get in Touch \342\200\224 Dedicated support desk for setup, spreadsheet data migration, and onboarding. Reach out at hello@silsila.app.\nSection 10: Final CTA Banner\nBackground: --primary (Deep Forest Teal - dark mode) with a subtle radial grid pattern.\nLayout: Centered, highly impactful column block.\nMain Heading: \"Ready to reduce the chasing?\" (2.5rem, color #FFFFFF)\nSubheading: \"Join other madrasahs who are freeing up time, improving family communication, and securing fees.\"\nForm/CTAs:\nLarge Primary Mint Button: \"Book a 15-min demo\"\nAdjacent Outline Button: \"Contact Onboarding\"\nSection 11: Page Footer\nBackground: --background with top border 1px solid var(--border)\nLayout: Two-column flex split.\nLeft: Silsila logo + by Sylergy. \"Modern supplementary school administration, made simple.\"\nRight: \"Built with \360\237\222\232 by Sylergy. \302\251 2026 Silsila. All rights reserved.\"\n4. Engineering & Code Execution Guidelines\nWhen feeding this file to an AI developer model (e.g., in Google AI Studio), include this prompt constraint:\n\nEnsure the See it in action component has reactive JavaScript states so that clicking individual tabs alters both the text block on the left and the interactive table/dashboard mockup on the right.\nEnsure all margins, padding values, and grids strictly scale using Tailwind utilities that correspond to the spacing rules: --space-element (gap-10 or space-y-10), --space-block (my-20 or space-y-20), and --space-section (py-24 or py-32).\nTailwind configurations must extend the color variables mapped in Section 1.B for uniform color rendering across screens.\n"
    items {
      text: "Silsila Maktab \342\200\224 Full-Page Landing Page Design Specification (v2)\nThis document represents the complete, high-fidelity design specification for the Silsilah Maktab landing page. It combines the core design system tokens (colors, typography, buttons, tables, badges, cards, and scrollbars) with the actual page sections, layouts, and copy transcribed from the full-page product landing page screenshot.\n\nUse this specification in Google AI Studio to generate a pixel-perfect, responsive, and highly interactive landing page using HTML/Tailwind CSS or React/Tailwind CSS.\n\n1. Brand Identity & Global Style Tokens\nA. Design System Concept\nProduct Name: Silsila Maktab (branded as Silsila by Sylergy)\nTheme: Minimalist, serene, highly professional, and modern administrative software for supplementary Islamic schools (Maktabs/Madrasahs).\nCore Aesthetic: Warm off-white backgrounds, deep forest-green primary containers, and bright mint-green accents that promote feelings of growth, heritage, structure, and peace.\nB. Color Palette\nImplement these exact custom property mappings:\n\n:root {\n  --primary: #1D564B;       /* Deep Forest Green/Teal - primary headers, main cards, hero buttons */\n  --accent: #00A896;        /* Bright Mint/Teal - brand highlights, badges, primary CTA backgrounds */\n  --background: #FBF9F6;    /* Off-white/Warm Cream - global body background */\n  --card: #FFFFFF;          /* Pure White - background for elevated container components and cards */\n  --secondary: #EEEAE5;     /* Warm Light Grey - background for alternating sections or inactive elements */\n  --muted: #E5E0DA;         /* Muted Soft Grey - for subtle borders, secondary labels, and text */\n  --border: #E1DCD6;        /* Outer Structural Borders - thin card lines and table grid lines */\n  --destructive: #D9383A;   /* Overdue Red - for negative alerts, overdue invoices, and \"Absent\" statuses */\n}\nC. Typography Scale\nFont Family: Modern, highly readable sans-serif (e.g., Plus Jakarta Sans, Inter, or Outfit).\nHero Title: 3.5rem (56px) / Weight 600 / Line-height 1.2\nSection Heading: 2.25rem (36px) / Weight 600 / Line-height 1.3\nBody / Paragraph: 1.125rem (18px) / Weight 400 / Line-height 1.6\nMuted / Small: 0.875rem (14px) / Weight 400 / Line-height 1.4\nD. Spacing & Grid System\nElement Padding (--space-element): 2.5rem (40px) \342\200\224 internal card gaps, button spacing, form fields.\nBlock Grid Gap (--space-block): 5rem (80px) \342\200\224 vertical margins between columns and groups of cards.\nSection Gap (--space-section): 8.5rem (136px) \342\200\224 vertical padding (py-24 or py-32 in Tailwind) separating main page sections.\n2. Reusable UI Components\nA. Buttons & CTAs\nPrimary Mint CTA (Main Landing Page Button):\nSolid --accent background, text #FFFFFF (or dark forest green if contrast warrants). Hover: background --accent with opacity 0.9, scale up slightly on hover.\nSecondary Green CTA (Standard Action Button):\nSolid --primary background, text #FFFFFF. Hover: slight background change, smooth transition.\nOutline Button:\nTransparent background, border 1.5px solid var(--primary), text --primary.\nGhost Button:\nTransparent background, text --primary. Hover: background --secondary.\nDestructive Button:\nSolid --destructive background, text #FFFFFF. Sizes:\nDefault (Navbar/Standard): padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem; font-size: 16px;\nLarge (Hero/Banner): padding: 0.875rem 1.75rem; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600;\nB. Cards & Elevating Containers\nBasic Card: --card background, 1px solid var(--border), rounded corners (12px / 0.75rem).\nFeature Card (Hoverable): Same as basic card but on hover applies box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(29, 86, 75, 0.04) and translates translate-y-[-4px] upwards.\nHighlighted Card: Pure white card with solid border accent border-top: 4px solid var(--accent) or border-left: 4px solid var(--primary).\nC. Status Badges & Attendance Markers\nTo display administrative capabilities, mock indicators must use these exact styling formulas:\n\nPaid (Success Badge): pill style, bg #EBF7EE, border #C3EBD0, text #1E562A, label \"Paid\"\nPending (Warning Badge): pill style, bg #FFF8EC, border #FFE3B3, text #8A5E1A, label \"Pending\"\nOverdue (Destructive Badge): pill style, bg #FDF2F2, border #FAD2D2, text #9C2A2B, label \"Overdue\"\nAttendance Dot (Present - P): Circle, bg #EBF7EE, text #1E562A, font-bold, label \"P\"\nAttendance Dot (Absent - A): Circle, bg #FDF2F2, text #9C2A2B, font-bold, label \"A\"\nAttendance Dot (Late - L): Circle, bg #FFF8EC, text #8A5E1A, font-bold, label \"L\"\n3. Core Page Sections (Layout & Copy)\nImplement the landing page in a vertical sequence using the sections below. Alternating background colors are noted for visual depth.\n\nSection 1: Navigation Header (Sticky)\nBackground: --background (fully transparent on scroll with backdrop-blur)\nLayout: Centered, max-width wrapper with flex space-between.\nLogo (Left): Minimalist wordmark: Silsila (font-semibold, --primary, 1.5rem) + <span class=\"text-xs text-accent\">by Sylergy</span>.\nNav Links (Center): Product, Use Cases, Pricing, About, Staff Login, Parent Login, Register school.\nCTA (Right): Small \"Book a 15-min demo\" button in Primary Mint (--accent).\nSection 2: Hero Fold (Value Proposition & Mock Dashboard)\nBackground: --background\nLayout: Two-column layout (stacks to single-column on mobile).\nLeft Column (Text & Action):\nCategory Badge: Centered or left-aligned light pill text: FOR MADRASAHS & MAKTABS (text --accent, tracking-wider, font-bold).\nMain Heading: \"Attendance and fees, finally under control.\" (size 3.5rem, weight 600, color --primary).\nSubheading: \"Reduce admin time, collect fees faster, and give every family a reliable portal\342\200\224budget gently by WhatsApp.\"\nInline Bullet List (with checkmark icons):\n\342\234\224 Proofing registry in minutes, not hours\n\342\234\224 Verifiably faster with fewer follow-ups\n\342\234\224 Partners with standard WhatsApp and emails\nCTA Block:\nButton 1: \"Book a 15-min demo\" (Large Primary Mint Button)\nButton 2: \"See the parent portal \342\206\222\" (Ghost button with chevron arrow)\nRight Column (Dashboard Preview):\nAn interactive CSS mockup of the Silsila Administrator Dashboard:\nHeader: \"Dashboard \342\200\224 Monday, 11 Nov 2024\"\nStats Row:\nAttendance Rate: 94% (with small green sparkline or trend badge)\nFees Collected: \302\2436,280 (progress bar at 85%)\nUnpaid Invoices: \302\243410 (colored red --destructive)\nTotal Pupils: 121\nRecent Activity List:\nZahra Rahman attended Year 3 - Qur\'an (timestamp: 10 mins ago)\nFaisal Ahmed marked Late for Year 1\nFees paid for Adam Rahman (\302\24345.00)\nMonthly automated invoices generated\nSection 3: Social Proof / Testimonials Band\nBackground: --secondary (creates a soft break from the hero background)\nLayout: Clean grid of 2 prominent blockquote feature cards side-by-side.\nCard 1 Quote:\n\"Virtually, a system that understands how madrasahs actually work. The WhatsApp integration is a superb change for parent communication!\"\nAuthor: Ustadh Bilal Vance, Head Teacher, Madrasah Al-Ansar\nCard 2 Quote:\n\"We recovered our fee-chasing time significantly. Parents can give their details and look up invoices through the portal seamlessly.\"\nAuthor: Fihan Rahman, Madrasah Treasurer\nSection 4: Problem vs. Solution (\"From Chaos to Calm\")\nBackground: --primary (Deep Forest Teal - dark mode section with white text)\nHeader:\nWHAT WE SOLVE (Small, --accent uppercase label)\n\"From chaos to calm\" (Section Heading 2.25rem, color #FFFFFF)\nSubtitle: \"Madrasah admin shouldn\'t feel overwhelming. Silsila replaces fragmented tools with one simple system\342\200\224one class at a time.\"\nLayout: Two-column layout contrasting the traditional challenges vs Silsila\'s modern workflows.\nLeft Column (The Problem):\nRed accent flags:\n\342\235\214 Information stored across too many apps: Paper registers, personal WhatsApp threads, and fragile spreadsheets make tracking a heavy chore.\n\342\235\214 Fee-chasing is a constant chore: Unclear balances, missed payment deadlines, and awkward, repeating face-to-face follow-up conversations.\n\342\235\214 Parent communication feels chaotic: Crucial school updates get lost in endless community group chats; parents are left in the dark about attendance and pending invoices.\nRight Column (Silsila\'s Approach):\nGreen/Mint accent flags:\n\342\234\224 One unified, cloud-based platform: A single, beautiful web application accessible securely from any device, anytime.\n\342\234\224 Clear invoices and easy payments: Automated WhatsApp and SMS payment links with instant, elegant receipt generation.\n\342\234\224 A modern web portal for families: Parents log in with passwordless magic links to view historical attendance records, upcoming schedules, and invoices.\nSection 5: \"Built for how madrasahs work\" (The Feature Grid)\nBackground: --background\nHeader:\nTHE TOOLKIT (Small, --accent uppercase label)\n\"Built for how madrasahs work\"\nSubtitle: \"Every feature is shaped around a real workflow\342\200\224one that turns a daily administrative headache into a beautiful, quiet routine.\"\nGrid Layout: 3-column, 2-row grid of Feature Cards (Hoverable).\nCards Content:\nFast Attendance Register: Pupil registers completed in under a minute, optimized for fast mobile or desktop clicking.\nInteractive Core Stats: Access parent details, emergency contact numbers, medical notes, and classroom schedules instantly.\nInvoicing and Analysis: Generate clean receipts, track physical cash vs bank transfers, and see exactly who has paid at a glance.\nWhatsApp & SMS Links: Deliver direct payment links straight to parent phones, drastically lowering late-payment frequency.\nParent Portal: Passwordless login links let parents track attendance charts, pay fees, and view active announcements on their own.\nAudit Trails & Reports: Every invoice adjustment, fee collection, or attendance status change is timestamped and ready to export.\nSection 6: Interactive Showcase (\"See it in action\")\nBackground: --primary (Deep Forest Teal - dark mode)\nHeader:\nIN ACTION (Small, --accent uppercase label)\n\"See it in action\"\nSubtitle: \"Three perspectives, one system. Admin, teachers, and parents\342\200\224each get exactly what they need.\"\nInteractive Component:\nHorizontal selection bar representing three perspective tabs:\nTab 1: Staff - Take Attendance (Active by default)\nTab 2: Admin - Invoice + Pay Desk\nTab 3: Parent View - Fee Portal\nDynamic Content Layout:\nLeft column (Perspective copy):\nTitle: \"Mark attendance in seconds\"\nBullets:\nSee pupil class history instantly\nTap once to toggle present, absent, or late\nSubmit with one tap \342\200\224 register is automatically locked and shared with admin\nRight column (Simulated Interactive Component Mockup):\nRender the Dense Table (Weekly Attendance Grid) with custom badge status selectors:\nAdam Rahman | Mon: P | Tue: P | Wed: L | Thu: P | Fri: P\nZahra Rahman | Mon: P | Tue: A | Wed: P | Thu: P | Fri: P\nFeatures a large, solid --accent button: \"Submit Attendance Register\".\nSection 7: Proof & Quantitative Metrics (\"Fee chasing, cut by 70%\")\nBackground: --background\nHeader:\nEARLY RESULTS\n\"Fee chasing, cut by 70%\"\nSubtitle: \"Early pilots show a significant drop in administrative hours and immediate boosts to fee collection compliance.\"\nGrid of Supporting Pilot Testimonial Cards:\nCard 1: \"The attendance register is so quick now. It takes us under a minute to check in all the students.\" (\342\200\223 Teacher, Year 3)\nCard 2: \"Prior to this, we spent hours chasing invoices manually. The WhatsApp links make paying effortless for parents.\" (\342\200\223 Administrator, Al-Kauthar Academy)\nCard 3: \"I love being able to see everything on the portal\342\200\224attendance, schedules, and my invoices. No more mystery.\" (\342\200\223 Parent, Year 1 Pupil)\nSection 8: \"Simple, transparent pricing\"\nBackground: --secondary\nHeader:\nPRICING\n\"Simple, transparent pricing\"\nSubtitle: \"Pick the plan that fits your school. Prices are simple\342\200\224book a demo and we\'ll tailor it for your custom numbers.\"\nLayout: Grid of 3 pricing cards. Highlight the center card (Standard) to make it stand out.\nTiers:\nStarter (For small, newly established weekend schools)\nPrice: \302\24329 / month\nFeatures: Up to 50 active students, Daily attendance register, Basic reporting, Standard email support.\nCTA: \"Book a 15-min demo \342\206\222\" (Outline Button)\nStandard (Most Popular - Featured)\nVisuals: Primary accent header border (border-top: 4px solid var(--accent)), subtle drop shadow.\nPrice: \302\24349 / month\nFeatures: Up to 150 active students, Advanced attendance registry, Automated invoicing & tracking, WhatsApp/SMS direct payment links, Basic family dashboard, Priority email/phone support.\nCTA: \"Book a 15-min demo \342\206\222\" (Solid Primary Mint Button)\nPro (For large schools and established Madrasah networks)\nPrice: \302\24399 / month\nFeatures: Unlimited active students, Everything in Standard, Automated invoice reminders, Multi-site campus support, Custom integrations, Dedicated onboarding account manager.\nCTA: \"Book a 15-min demo \342\206\222\" (Outline Button)\nSection 9: \"A chain unbroken\" (Philosophy & Mission)\nBackground: --background\nHeader:\nOUR MISSION\n\"A chain unbroken\"\nSubtitle: \"Silsilah means an unbroken chain\342\200\224the link between family, teacher, and madrasah. We build tools to strengthen this connection, so teachers can focus on teaching.\"\nLayout: 3-column block detailing values:\nColumn 1: Deep Tradition, Modern Tech \342\200\224 Designed by developers who have run Maktabs, bridging classic Islamic supplementary school dynamics with streamlined web workflows.\nColumn 4: Low Connectivity Friendly \342\200\224 Highly optimized client-side code that works gracefully on weak mobile cellular connections or older parent devices.\nColumn 5: Get in Touch \342\200\224 Dedicated support desk for setup, spreadsheet data migration, and onboarding. Reach out at hello@silsila.app.\nSection 10: Final CTA Banner\nBackground: --primary (Deep Forest Teal - dark mode) with a subtle radial grid pattern.\nLayout: Centered, highly impactful column block.\nMain Heading: \"Ready to reduce the chasing?\" (2.5rem, color #FFFFFF)\nSubheading: \"Join other madrasahs who are freeing up time, improving family communication, and securing fees.\"\nForm/CTAs:\nLarge Primary Mint Button: \"Book a 15-min demo\"\nAdjacent Outline Button: \"Contact Onboarding\"\nSection 11: Page Footer\nBackground: --background with top border 1px solid var(--border)\nLayout: Two-column flex split.\nLeft: Silsila logo + by Sylergy. \"Modern supplementary school administration, made simple.\"\nRight: \"Built with \360\237\222\232 by Sylergy. \302\251 2026 Silsila. All rights reserved.\"\n4. Engineering & Code Execution Guidelines\nWhen feeding this file to an AI developer model (e.g., in Google AI Studio), include this prompt constraint:\n\nEnsure the See it in action component has reactive JavaScript states so that clicking individual tabs alters both the text block on the left and the interactive table/dashboard mockup on the right.\nEnsure all margins, padding values, and grids strictly scale using Tailwind utilities that correspond to the spacing rules: --space-element (gap-10 or space-y-10), --space-block (my-20 or space-y-20), and --space-section (py-24 or py-32).\nTailwind configurations must extend the color variables mapped in Section 1.B for uniform color rendering across screens.\n"
    }
  }
}
